{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWy7BaVTzZdNj7sgqrFCAU","type":"tool_result","content":"internal/servecmd/serve.go:84:// knownLoops are the names registerLoops' loops report (Loop.Name), in the\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go:86:var knownLoops = []string{\"scanners\", stale.Name, \"triage\", \"workers\", \"reviewers\", \"reviewfix\", \"merger\", \"reaper\"}\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go:98:\t\tif !slices.Contains(knownLoops, n) {\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go:99:\t\t\treturn nil, &cli.ExitError{Code: 2, Err: fmt.Errorf(\"ard serve: --loops: unknown loop %q (known: %s)\", n, strings.Join(knownLoops, \", \"))}\ninternal/servecmd/adopt.go:57:// when non-nil, is the pool's Options.Limited: it keeps candidates whose\ninternal/servecmd/adopt.go:65:\treturn pool.New(pool.Options{Max: maxPods, Held: held, Log: log, Limited: limited}), nil\ninternal/servecmd/reaping.go:158:// limitedFor is the pool's Options.Limited: when a candidate may next start\ninternal/costs/rows.go:59:\tcase closeout.OutcomeLimited:\ninternal/state/jobs.go:598:// FailLimited is Fail for a job that stopped at a usage limit: status stays\ninternal/state/jobs.go:603:func (s *Store) FailLimited(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error {\ninternal/closeout/comment.go:79:\tcase OutcomeLimited:\ninternal/closeout/comment.go:106:\tif p.Outcome != OutcomeFailed && p.Outcome != OutcomeRetry && p.Outcome != OutcomeLimited {\ninternal/closeout/comment.go:112:\tif p.Outcome == OutcomeLimited {\ninternal/closeout/plan.go:29:\t// OutcomeLimited is a stop at a subscription usage limit. Its labels are\ninternal/closeout/plan.go:33:\tOutcomeLimited Outcome = \"usage-limit\"\ninternal/closeout/plan.go:178:// and adds no terminal label. What differs is the state change (FailLimited)\ninternal/closeout/plan.go:182:\tp.Outcome = OutcomeLimited\ninternal/closeout/closeout.go:24:// Cause.ResetsAt, OutcomeLimited) and Job.Home: older records decode them as zero, and