t64\n\tBudgetUSDPerDay float64\n}\n\n// ReadsUntrusted reports whether the role's job reads untrusted input (issue\n// bodies, comments, PR text, diffs): every triage, worker and reviewer role,\n// and an LLM scanner. Only a deterministic scanner (an executable `scan`)\n// does not. A scanner without ScanPath counts as LLM, so the check fails closed.\nfunc (r Role) ReadsUntrusted() bool { return r.Kind != KindScanner || r.ScanPath == \"\" }\n28:## Layout\n29-\n30-Packages are created as their issues land; keep this list current.\n31-\n32-```\n33-cmd/ard/            CLI entry point; wire a new subcommand by adding one line to handlers()\n34-internal/cli/       cobra command tree, global flags, slog logging; Handlers is the plug-in point\n35-internal/botcheck/  tests for the bot-commit audit in .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\n36-internal/github/    GitHub client: domain types, Reader/Writer/Client, App auth, retry transport; query/ (search builder), fake/ (test double), clienttest/ (conformance suite)\n37-internal/config/    .ard/config.yaml + role directory loading into a Resolved value (pure, fs.FS in)\n38-internal/configcmd/ `ard config check` handler: prints the resolved config, returns validation errors; `--ref` checks a commit\n39-internal/configsrc/  config from origin/main: a snapshot per SHA under ~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/ (what `ard serve` reads)\n40-internal/executor/    Executor interface and plain-data job types\n41-internal/executor/local/  git worktree + host subprocess or docker run, watchdog, logs\n42-internal/agent/     Adapter interface, Spec/Result types, Registry (pure: builds argv, parses output)\n43-internal/agent/claude/  Claude Code adapter (`claude -p`, stream-json parser)\n44-internal/modelauth/ picks the one model credential (OAuth token or API key) from the controller env and carries its value to the executor; never logged\n45-internal/state/     SQLite controller and scanner state (sqlitex, scannerdb)\n46-internal/scanner/   scanne